			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Clean up dead vars and normalize scan paths lexically\n\nReplace the filesystem-backed `Canonicalize` closure in ScanPathConfigure\nwith `Normalize`, which resolves `..` segments lexically for non-existent\npaths - keeping extension scan-path log output clean regardless of path\nviability - while still calling `std::fs::canonicalize` for existing paths\nto resolve symlinks.\n\nDrop the stale `HandleSlot` accumulator in OutputChannelCoalesce (it was\nset but never meaningfully used after the previous refactor) and the\nunused `std::path::PathBuf` import in TryShipped.\n\nAdd stub IPC handlers for `browserView:*` (updateKeybindings, updateTheme,\nupdateConfiguration, openDevTools, closeDevTools -> Null;\ngetBrowserViews -> []), which Wind sends for Electron BrowserView\nmanagement but are no-ops under Tauri's single-webview architecture.\nRoute `extensionHostStarter:waitForExit` to a new async handler that\nresolves immediately with a stub exit-info so callers don't hang.\n\nFormatting-only: line-break Cocoon environment allow list one-per-entry,\ncollapse LocalhostUrl accessors, reflow WebviewWindowBuilder chain.",
			"SHA": "167dfea1480a374254428bcbbafa11c6113041c5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T08:36:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1585,
				7
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Serve webview panels via localhost plugin URL\n\nSecondary webview panels (settings, webview extensions, etc.) used `WebviewUrl::App(\"WebviewHost.html\")` which routes through tauri::manager — but Mountain's tauri.conf.json has no `frontendDist`, so Tauri has no bundled assets to serve, leaving those webviews blank.\n\nFix by loading them from the localhost plugin instead (`http://localhost:PORT/Mountain/WebviewHost`). A new `LocalhostUrl` singleton (OnceLock in `IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Utilities/LocalhostUrl.rs`) is populated once during `AppLifecycleSetup` and consumed in `create_webview_panel_impl` to build the external URL. Falls back to port 15536 if the singleton is unset.\n\nAlso extracts the inline Cocoon subprocess environment-building and I/O forwarding into named functions (`BuildCocoonEnvironment`, `SpawnCocoonIoForwarders`) in CocoonManagement.rs — pure refactor with no behavioral change, reducing method complexity from ~200 inline lines to two clear helpers.",
			"SHA": "88be9db9ea1de55af0b96158021b2b77c7f86f6c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T07:49:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1582,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Enable .app bundle resource resolution for cache, Cocoon, and Node\n\nThe Mountain binary now resolves pre-baked resources from both the repo/dev\nlayout (binary-sibling files) and the .app bundle layout (Contents/Resources/)\nwhen running as a packaged application. Four systems are updated:\n\n**Extension manifest cache (LoadFromCache.rs):** Probes two locations in\norder — `BinaryDir/extensions.manifest.json` (dev) and\n`BinaryDir/../Resources/extensions.manifest.json` (bundle). Bundled caches\nskip the staleness check (10-minute threshold) since they are built\nalongside the .app and always consistent with its packed extensions. The\nper-manifest field extraction is also refactored with local `str()` and\n`arr()` helper closures to eliminate repeated\n`Manifest.get(k).and_then(Value::as_str)` chains.\n\n**CocoonManagement pre-flight check:** Cocoon's bundle probe now attempts\nTauri's resource resolver first (`Tauri::path::resolve` with\n`BaseDirectory::Resource`), falling back to the repo-layout relative-walk\nfrom `scripts/cocoon/` when the bundle path does not exist.\n\n**NodeResolver TryShipped:** Adds a sidecar resolution path matching\n`externalBin: [\"Binary/node\"]` in tauri.conf.json — the `node` binary sits\nalongside the Mountain executable, not in a `Node/bin/` subdirectory, in\nthe Tauri sidecar layout.\n\n**ScanPathConfigure and PathSecurity:** Extension scan paths now call\n`.canonicalize()` on resolved paths for cleaner log output (showing\n`Contents/Resources/...` instead of `Contents/MacOS/../Resources/...`).\n`IsTrustedSystemPath` adds `../Resources/Static/Application/extensions` to\nthe bundle-root allowlist so the new canonical static extension directory\nbypasses the workspace-folder gate.\n\n**Bootstrap fork (bootstrap-fork.js):** Cocoon entry path resolution\nhandles both bundle (2-level `../../`) and repo (3-level `../../../`)\nlayouts by iterating both URL bases for each candidate entry path.\n\n**tauri.conf.json:** Maps `bootstrap-fork.js`, `extensions.manifest.json`,\nand `Cocoon/Target/Bootstrap/Implementation/Cocoon` into\n`Contents/Resources/` so all three are reachable at runtime via the bundle\nresource resolver.",
			"SHA": "0fe6cbfa5522594264233b21f4807ab5f184dab4"
		},
