			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Normalize extension location URI from cache to plain string\n\nThe `LoadFromCache` path serialized `ExtensionLocation` as a JSON object\n`{\"value\": url}` — the Identifier wrapper shape — rather than a plain\n`Value::String` URI. The `Normalize.rs` URI parser then failed to match\nagainst the `scheme` key and fell through to `/extensions/unknown`,\nbreaking extension resolution for cached manifests.\n\n- Fix the source: emit `Value::String(LocationUri)` from\n  `LoadFromCache.rs`, matching the format `FromUrl::Fn` expects.\n- Fix the sink: add a backward-compatibility branch in `Normalize.rs`\n  that unwraps `{\"value\": url_string}` when encountered, so legacy\n  cache entries still resolve correctly.\n- Reorder Sky resource globs in `tauri.conf.json` alphabetically for\n  maintainability.\n\nAccompanying build metadata: the Cargo.toml package name, tauri\nidentifier, and productName are expanded to their full environment-keyed\nform (DevelopmentNodeEnvironment…) as part of the CI artifact\nlabelling scheme; backup files preserve the canonical values.",
			"SHA": "af8fcdd2e74f49cd5943e056f6af38bddb0d7205"
		}
	],
